		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3569#p3569"><![CDATA[
You can directly change the position for tree structures, working from the root out to the leaves. For systems with cycles (loops) you might have convergence problems. It's really a nonlinear problem.<br><br>In a sense Baumgarte stabilization is directly modifying position, but in a relaxed, sequential manner.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Wed Feb 21, 2007 6:39 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
