		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3548#p3548"><![CDATA[
There are a couple things you can do to improve the position resolution for inequality constraints:<br><br>- Use some position slop. Don't apply Baumgarte unless the position error is greater than the slop value. This should get rid of jitter.<br>- Use a separate solver for position error. This can be in the form of pseudo velocities that don't affect the momentum. This will eliminate momentum gain and make the simulation a bit more stable.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Tue Feb 20, 2007 10:29 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
